Z||000000||ThatRickGuy||07-12-2000||07:08 AM||||Hey there, a continuance of "expencive" with a new angle. I read threw almost everything in the search under 3.4 swap,  but there was very little coverage for an '88 2.8 w/ auto to the 3.4. <P>Things I'm still a little fuzzy on:<BR>1.Is the block grinding/remounting for the starter something that could be acheived w/ out a machine shop? <P>2.What about the flex plate, I've heard talk of needing and earlier or later neutrally balanced one.<P>3. Engine mount, I head that you could use the 88 but you have to grind off the side bolt hole on the front side.<P>4. A/C bracket, I head something about having to weld a bolt to the block to act as a stud, true of false?<P>5. Any other mods or insightfull knowledge?<P>I'm just trying to get everything priced out to compare my options. Thanks again.||||reg||5
Z||000001||ThatRickGuy||07-12-2000||07:10 AM||||oh yeah, the 3.4 I'm refering to is the pushrod camero engine, and the fiero is an '88 formula.||||reg||1
Z||000002||batboy||07-12-2000||07:11 AM|||| <A HREF="http://www.angelfire.com/on/fierofactory/start.html#34" TARGET=_blank>http://www.angelfire.com/on/fierofactory/start.html#34</A> ||||reg||1
Z||000003||Alex4mula||07-12-2000||08:37 AM||||I did a 3.4 in my Formula with 5 spd.<BR>#3 is true. You need to cut about an inch or inch & half of that portion.<BR>#4 regarding the A/C you need a pre 88 A/C bracket which is just a little shorter and a pre 88 modified engine shock mount to get that bolt (& correct alignment) to mount it. 88's does not use that shock-to-cradle thing.<BR>On the Auto tranny I can't help too much. Call Ed Parks at Fiero Factory.||||reg||1
